    "register_notes_en": "C2 biography-and-work analysis: distinguish Werkimmanenz (Kayser, Staiger) / biographism (Dilthey tradition) / productive double-move (post-1970 Konstanz school plus Bourdieu). Theoretical anchors: Barthes 'Death of the Author', Foucault 'What Is an Author?', Bourdieu 'biographical illusion'. Konjunktiv I for citing theory: 'Bourdieu zufolge sei die Biographie als nachträgliche Konstruktion zu begreifen'. Funktionsverbgefüge: 'hinter den Text setzen' (place behind the text), 'als analytischen Gegenstand fassen' (treat as analytical object), 'in Anschluss an X arbeiten' (work in the line of X). Source status has to be reflected on: diary ≠ letter ≠ essay ≠ third-party source. Self-mythologisation (Goethe's 'Dichtung und Wahrheit', Mann's diaries, Kafka's letters) must be handled critically, not naively. Avoid 'X IS the author' (identification); avoid 'biography explains the work' (causal short-circuit). Key formula: 'productive difference as the analytical object — biographical work as complementary, not substitutive perspective'.",
